{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 2, :comments ["<b>And the bull of the sin-offering and the two rams.</b> He placed the bull of the sin-offering first, as the Sages of blessed memory said: every sin-offering precedes the burnt-offering that comes with it, for until the sin is atoned for there is no place at all for a burnt-offering, as it says: עוֹלָה וְחַטָּאָה לֹא שָׁאָלְתָּ (Psalms 40:7). And his sin-offering after his anointing was a bull according to the law of the anointed priest, but its blood did not enter within, because his sin was not at the degree of errancy to require that, as was necessary for the ruling of the anointed priest (Leviticus 4:3) and the ruling of the court that caused error (Leviticus 4:13), and the bull and goat of the Day of Atonement, which atone for defilement of the Temple and for sins, transgressions, and rebellions, as is explained in the passage (Leviticus 16). And he placed the burnt-offering before the ordination-offerings, for in the burnt-offering too there is some atonement, as it says: וְנִרְצָה לוֹ לְכַפֵּר עָלָיו (Leviticus 1:4), and after the perfection of atonement they became fit to fill their hands to bring them to completion for the service."], :book :leviticus, :voice :sforno, :lang :en, :chapter 8, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-22T16:35:58.371527217Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}